{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "note": "Runner semantics: start from uikit/amity-uikit-config.json, deep-merge `configOverrides` on top (plain objects merge recursively key-by-key; arrays and scalars REPLACE wholesale — no concatenation), then resolve `token` for `scope`+`mode` using the schema_version 3 chain: semantic[token][mode] -> ref \"{AliasName}\"(@alpha:x)? or hex literal -> alias[AliasName] must be strictly \"{theme.<key>}\" -> resolve theme key through the per-scope cascade (exact \"page/component/element\" -> \"*/component/*\" -> \"page/*/*\" -> global theme.<mode>.<key>), each theme-block reading validated as strict 6/8-digit hex (a value present but not valid hex is skipped, falling through to the next cascade level) -> apply @alpha if present (overwrites any existing alpha byte, clamping alpha to [0,1] with a console.warn if out of range) -> hex is always uppercased. Missing at any step (absent token, unparseable ref, absent/malformed alias, or theme key missing at every cascade level including global) yields {value:\"#FF00FF\", source:\"missing\"}. The table is uikit/amity-uikit-design-tokens.json verbatim, EXCEPT vectors carrying the optional `tableOverrides` field: deep-merge it into the table the same way (used only to inject synthetic semantic cells for the unknown-alias and out-of-range-@alpha cases, which the shipping table cannot legally contain). Compare BOTH expected.value and expected.source. Sources: \"literal\" | \"theme:<key>@global\" | \"theme:<key>@scope:<matchedPattern>\" | \"missing\".",
